  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "A rectangle has area $20$. The width is $2+\\sqrt3$. Find the length of the rectangle in simplest form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$40-20\\sqrt3$\n\nDivide the area by the width, then rationalise using the conjugate.",
      "worked": "Using $A=lw$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}l&=\\frac{20}{2+\\sqrt3}\\\\l&=\\frac{20(2-\\sqrt3)}{(2+\\sqrt3)(2-\\sqrt3)}\\\\l&=\\frac{40-20\\sqrt3}{4-3}\\\\l&=40-20\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
